# Generated pipeline artifacts, not source -- every run overwrites these, and a Google
# Maps/Gemini API-call failure embeds the live key in its own error text (see
# planning.agent._redact_api_keys), so a committed log/output snapshot is a live
# credential leak waiting to happen (confirmed 2026-09-22: both GOOGLE_API_KEY and
# GEMINI_API_KEY were found leaked in the then-tracked logs/tuff.log, matching the
# .env values active at the time -- those keys need rotating). Untracked from git the
# same day; still written to disk exactly as before, just no longer part of the repo.
output/
logs/
